1
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:09,400
A garden is 15 sixteenths of an acre.

2
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:14,460
8 ninths of it is lawn, and 3 tenths of the lawn is reseeded.

3
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:16,930
What fraction of an acre is reseeded?

4
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:20,400
Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.

5
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:23,930
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,240
Cancel before you multiply.

7
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:28,730
3 and 9, 8 and 16, 15 and 10.

8
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:31,390
Everything cancels to 1 over 4.

9
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,740
A quarter of an acre.

10
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:39,420
Remember: to multiply fractions, multiply the tops, and multiply the bottoms.

11
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:42,910
2 thirds times 4 fifths is 8 fifteenths.

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:48,770
Before multiplying, cancel any top number with any bottom number that share a factor.

13
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:53,520
The numbers stay small, and the answer is already simplified.

14
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:56,150
A whole number N is N over 1.

15
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:56,880
Your turn.

16
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,000
Work out 18 times 5 twelfths.

17
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:02,790
Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.

18
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:06,160
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:13,150
Cancel 18 and 12 by 6: 3 times 5 halves is 15 halves, or 7 and a half.

20
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,820
For mixed numbers, change them to improper fractions first.

21
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:19,190
Here is the method.

22
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:23,850
Step 1: change mixed numbers and integers into fractions.

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,900
Step 2: cancel common factors, top with bottom.

24
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:31,530
Step 3: multiply the tops and the bottoms.

25
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:36,670
Step 4: change back to a mixed number if you need to, and estimate.

26
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:41,040
Work out 3 and 3 quarters, times 2 and 2 fifths.

27
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:44,310
That is 15 quarters times 12 fifths.

28
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:49,040
Cancel 15 and 5, and 12 and 4: 3 times 3 is 9.

29
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:49,790
Your turn.

30
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:53,240
Work out 2 and 2 thirds, times 1 and 1 eighth.

31
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:56,280
Pause and work it out.

32
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:58,350
8 thirds times 9 eighths.

33
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,670
Cancel the 8s, and 9 with 3.

34
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,000
The answer is 3.

35
00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:04,700
Estimate: about 3 times 1.

36
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:11,020
5 eighths of 2 and 2 fifths kilograms: 5 eighths times 12 fifths is 3 halves.

37
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:14,110
That is 1 and a half kilograms.

38
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,000
Leo works out 2 thirds plus 3 quarters.

39
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:19,030
Which line is wrong?

40
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,140
Line 1 is wrong.

41
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:24,540
You can only cancel when you multiply, not when you add.

42
00:02:24,590 --> 00:02:30,590
Use a common denominator: 8 twelfths plus 9 twelfths is 17 twelfths.

43
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:35,550
Chefs scale recipes by multiplying every amount by the same fraction.

44
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:40,930
To make 3 quarters of a recipe, multiply each amount by 3 quarters.

45
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,220
One last question.

46
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:44,880
Work out 6 sevenths times 7 twelfths.

47
00:02:44,930 --> 00:02:48,610
Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.

48
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,950
Pause the video and answer.

49
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,330
Cancel the 7s, and 6 with 12.

50
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:56,610
The answer is a half.

51
00:02:56,660 --> 00:03:01,090
To remember: cancel top with bottom before multiplying.

52
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:02,560
Integers are over 1.

53
00:03:02,610 --> 00:03:06,050
Mixed numbers become improper fractions.

54
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,590
Only cancel when multiplying.

55
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,010
Estimate to check.

56
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:16,230
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.3 on Camday.
